		HYDRAT.HL
  Help file for hydration studies - - 1-Jun- 84
     One must use several disks for the data analysis.  Use UCFILL.F4
on the uc prog. dsk to get a cell filling schedule.  I have tried
(2954) using 9 sample distributed in 15 channels between 2 runs.  This
looks good except the temperature of the AnG rotor is hard to control.
     Collect the data with UCMPX and process is for M(dp/dc) with
SPROG and then SLOPD.  I have recently also developed SCEXFD for a
multiple exponential fit.  Data from several scans and fits are merged
with MERGSC.F4 and then averaged with AVSCOP.F4.  At the end of the
o.p. data file from this program are the sample #, Mw, and Mv data.
     One copies this set of data to a tape and switch to the HPLC disk.
Now make a file of % sucrose with the samples in the same order of the
samples in the rotor.  Use SUCBUF.F4 to get the g3,v3,(1-v1p),etc data.
Now use MERG.F4 to merge the g3, etc data with the U.C. data.  This
o.p. file is the one required by HYDMLE.F4 for determination of the
preferential hydration.  The optional o.p. file consists of g3,X1'*g3,
and Err.  PLTXY.LD on the HPLC system is used to plot the data.
Note that the error estimated in the MLE mode for HYDMLE is vastly
underestimated.  I dont know why.
